SUMMARY:Vulnerability can endure
DESCRIPTION:Julian of Norwich\n\nThe created thing is fragile\, contingent\
 , and still held in being\; dependence is not identical with worthlessness
 .\n\nJulian's confidence does not come from denying wounds. Her distinctiv
 e move is to deny them the final interpretive authority.\n\nCONVERSATION\n
 With Nicholas of Cusa (“Knowing has an asymptote”): one loosens the fi
 lters of perception\; the other loosens conceptual possession. Together th
 ey suggest that seeing more may require doing less with what appears.\n\nS
 ource: hazelnut vision.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
